# SOC Detection Use Cases

This document describes the security monitoring use cases implemented in the lab.

| Use Case | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| SSH Brute-Force Detection | Wazuh | Identify repeated failed SSH logins |
| Automated IP Blocking | Wazuh Active Response | Block matching source IP |
| Network Threat Monitoring | Suricata | Inspect network security events |
| File Modification Detection | Wazuh FIM | Identify file changes |
| File Deletion Detection | Wazuh FIM | Identify deleted files |
| Vulnerability Monitoring | Wazuh | Identify known software vulnerabilities |

## SOC Analyst Investigation Process

1. Review the generated alert.
2. Identify the source and destination.
3. Check timestamps and event details.
4. Determine severity and potential impact.
5. Review related security events.
6. Verify whether an automated response occurred.
7. Document investigation findings.
